  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Romanian doina free-rhythm extended-melismatic lament-and-pastoral solo vocal-or-instrumental tradition of Romania and Moldova. Performance: solo unaccompanied voice (or solo violin, solo wooden-flute caval, or solo wooden-clarinet) in characteristic free-rhythm parlando-rubato style with extensive ornamental-melismatic figuration on long vowels. The doina has multiple regional sub-traditions: doină de jale (lament-doina), doină ciobănească (shepherd-doina), doină haiducească (outlaw-doina), and doină de dragoste (love-doina), each with characteristic regional intonation conventions. Distinguished from broader Romanian folk-song by doina's strict free-rhythm extended-melismatic structural requirement.",
